From 97fd7dff0b860ea5e58aca9b09eda9c038c13c2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bluevisor <bluevisor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] kernel/arm64: user debugging: breakpoints, single step,
 traps

- Software breakpoints (brk #0x4842). With no hardware breakpoints to swap
  in, continuing from one takes it out, single-steps the thread over the
  original instruction and puts it back from the step trap.
- Single step through MDSCR_EL1.SS/PSTATE.SS; the OS lock is released
  per CPU, MDSCR_EL1.SS is only set while returning to a stepping thread.
- arch_set_debug_cpu_state(), arch_debug_get_interrupt_pc(), FP/SIMD
  registers in arm64_debug_cpu_state.
- Userland brk, undefined instructions, SP alignment and FP traps raise
  signals (and debugger events) instead of panicking the kernel.
- Sync the I-cache after the breakpoint manager writes code; fix the
  I-cache line size computation in arch_cpu_sync_icache().
